---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Team Leaders | Departure: Fitness Quest"
  description="Every 60 days, each Departure team elects a Team Leader. The leader earns 10% more XP and a coin bonus, and decides when the team fights its next monster."
  ogImage="/social/team-leader.jpg"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="pt-16 pb-12 lg:pt-24 lg:pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 text-center">
      <span class="text-gold text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">The Team Leader System</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl font-extrabold mt-3 mb-4">Lead the warband.</h1>
      <p class="text-text-muted text-lg max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Every strong team has someone who sets the pace. In Departure, the team votes for that person, called the
        Team Leader, and the leader earns rewards in the game for doing the job.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why it exists -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-surface/30">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <div>
          <span class="text-primary-light text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">Why it matters</span>
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-2 mb-4">Fitness teams need leaders.</h2>
          <p class="text-text-muted mb-4">
            Most team fitness apps give every member the same buttons and hope someone takes charge.
            Often nobody does, so the group chat goes quiet and people stop training.
          </p>
          <p class="text-text-muted">
            Departure gives that job to one person. The team elects a Team Leader, who has duties no one
            else has and rewards worth earning.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gold/30">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-gold/15 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gold" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M5 3a2 2 0 00-2 2v2a2 2 0 002 2h.5a.5.5 0 010 1H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v2a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-2a2 2 0 00-2-2h-.5a.5.5 0 010-1h.5a2 2 0 002-2V5a2 2 0 00-2-2H5z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">The Rewards</h3>
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-gold font-bold shrink-0">+10%</span>
              <span class="text-text-muted">The leader earns 10% more XP on every workout for the whole 60 day term. It adds to other XP boosts, such as the Starter or Elite Pack, up to a limit of 1.5 times normal XP.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-green font-bold shrink-0">Coins</span>
              <span class="text-text-muted">The new leader gets a signing bonus of 1,000 coins plus 100 coins for each team member, so a bigger team pays more.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-gold font-bold shrink-0">Crown</span>
              <span class="text-text-muted">A crown marks you as the leader on your profile and the team page for your whole term.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-blue-400 font-bold shrink-0">Override</span>
              <span class="text-text-muted">If the anti-cheat rules cut XP from a teammate's honest workout, the leader can give it back. Each override costs the leader 25 coins, and the whole team can see it.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Responsibilities -->
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <span class="text-primary-light text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">The Job</span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-2">What a leader actually does.</h2>
        <p class="text-text-muted mt-3 max-w-2xl mx-auto">The rewards come with work, and the team expects its leader to show up.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/5">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Advance the warpath</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm">The warpath is the team's journey map of 24 monsters, and only the leader can start a fight on it. If the leader does not show up, the team does not move forward.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/5">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Run the feed</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm">React to and comment on teammates' workouts to keep them going. The whole team sees what you do, and members remember it at the next election.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/5">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Recruit warriors</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm">Invite new members to grow the team. A bigger team means a bigger signing bonus for whoever the team elects next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/5">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Override fair fails</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm">The anti-cheat rules are strict on purpose, so they sometimes flag an honest workout. The leader can then restore its XP, and every override is recorded where the whole team can see it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Elections -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-surface/30">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <span class="text-gold text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">Elections</span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-2">Every 60 days. Every member votes.</h2>
        <p class="text-text-muted mt-3 max-w-2xl mx-auto">Each election takes one week. Candidates write a pitch of up to 280 characters, every member gets one vote, and the candidate with the most votes wins.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-5 border border-white/5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 bg-primary/20 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
            <span class="text-primary-light text-sm font-bold">1</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Nominations</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-xs">For 3 days, members can nominate themselves or a teammate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-5 border border-white/5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 bg-primary/20 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
            <span class="text-primary-light text-sm font-bold">2</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Campaign</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-xs">For the next 3 days, each candidate shares a pitch of up to 280 characters.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-5 border border-white/5">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 bg-primary/20 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
            <span class="text-primary-light text-sm font-bold">3</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Vote</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-xs">Members then have 1 day to vote, one vote each, and the most votes wins.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-5 border border-gold/30">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 bg-gold/15 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
            <span class="text-gold text-sm font-bold">4</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Coronation</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-xs">The new leader is announced, gets the signing bonus, and earns the XP boost for the next 60 days.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-center text-text-muted text-xs mt-6">
        A team needs at least 3 members to hold an election. Until then, the Steward runs the team.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Steward -->
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-500/20">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-slate-500/15 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-slate-300" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20"><path d="M5 3a2 2 0 00-2 2v2a2 2 0 002 2h.5a.5.5 0 010 1H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v2a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-2a2 2 0 00-2-2h-.5a.5.5 0 010-1h.5a2 2 0 002-2V5a2 2 0 00-2-2H5z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">The Steward</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-text-muted mb-3">
          If you create a team, you start as its Steward, a stand-in leader who has not been elected. You do the leader's
          work, such as starting battles, overriding unfair penalties and recruiting, and you earn the rewards only if the team elects you.
        </p>
        <p class="text-text-muted">
          Lead by example, and you can earn the crown.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Accountability -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-surface/30">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="text-center mb-10">
        <span class="text-blue-400 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">Accountability</span>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-2">Transparent by design.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/5">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Every override logged</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm">Every time a leader restores XP, the whole team can see who did it, when, and any note they left.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/5">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Recall an absent leader</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm">If the leader is inactive for 14 days, members can start a recall vote. The vote stays open for 48 hours, and if more than half the team votes yes, the leader's term ends.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-6 border border-white/5">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Resign freely</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm">A leader can step down at any time. The XP boost stops at once, the Steward takes over, and a new election starts within a week.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-4xl font-extrabold mb-4">Earn the crown.</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted text-lg mb-8">
        Join a team, train with them, and win the vote to lead the team for 60 days.
      </p>
      <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/id6761634387" class="inline-block bg-gradient-to-r from-primary to-primary-light text-white font-bold py-3 px-8 rounded-full hover:opacity-90 transition">
        Download Departure
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
